# private_inputs.sha256: every file of the owner's private input directory (SURV), by sha256, size in bytes and path.
# The files derive from the player's own ROM (translated code, packed worlds, disc staging trees, the ROM itself as
# iso_*/ROM.BIN): only these names, sizes and hashes are in the repository, never the files.
#
# Format: one file per line, "SHA256  SIZE  PATH", PATH relative to SURV; lines starting with # are comments.
# Check a copy, from the top of the repository (prints OK or FAILED per file):
#   awk '!/^#/ && NF == 3 {print $1 "  " $3}' ps1/rebuild/private_inputs.sha256 | (cd "$SURV" && sha256sum -c -)
# Compare what Track B regenerated (under TREE/out, same relative paths) with this list, SAME or DIFF per file present:
#   ROM=... SURV= ps1/rebuild/track_b_regenerate.sh TREE hashes
#   (kp/kplan.h and */rompages_P.pkl differ by design: the prepared tree has its own pad plan, the build writes the page lists)
# The ROM the inputs were made from is iso_*/ROM.BIN below (the untouched 8 MiB cartridge image).
# Sizes:
#   awk '!/^#/ && NF == 3 {print $2, $3}' ps1/rebuild/private_inputs.sha256 | (cd "$SURV" && while read n f; do [ "$(stat -c %s "$f")" = "$n" ] || echo "size differs: $f"; done)
